"fala" (speech): an answer of up to {words} words, to be heard.
{chatRules}
{speechRules}

prompt.sdd.teams.main:
Write the text that {theUser} will paste into {target} for the team daily, from the {ceremony} below.
{style}
Activities: {activities}
Decisions: {decisions}
Pending effects: {effects}

prompt.sdd.conflict.comment:
Issue {ref} was synced with main after a release. Rewrite the QA pipelines comment below, which will be edited in place.
Rules{rulesRef}: keep the text, the mention {qaMention} and the format;
replace the pipeline link with the PUSH pipeline of the merge commit{pipelinesHint};
add a line saying the branch was synced with main and whether it needs a retest, naming the overlapping files when there are any.
Do not invent a pipeline: if you cannot find the push one of the merge commit, keep the current one and say so in the summary.
Sync output:
{sync}
Tool unit: {unit}
Current comment:
{current}
"body": the complete comment, ready to replace the current one. "resumo" (summary): one sentence saying what changed.

prompt.sdd.conflict.ask:
{intro}
{ofUser} question (voice transcript): «{question}»
"fala" (speech): an answer of up to {words} words, to be heard.
{chatRules}
{speechRules}

prompt.sdd.gate.start:
Gate {gate} of issue {ref} ({title}), by voice. Read the artifact {file} in full (and what it cites, if you need to).
"resumo" (summary): the gate summary to be heard, up to {words} words: what the artifact concludes or proposes, the risks and what {theUser} is approving.
"perguntas" (questions): the quiz.
{quizRules}
{speechRules}

prompt.sdd.gate.rules:
Quiz rules{rulesRef}: up to {max} CONSEQUENCE questions ({kinds}), never a fact that a search could find;
each with 4 plausible options and one correct; the distractors come from real wrong readings of the artifact; never "all of the above", never an absurd one on purpose;
with more than {max} risk points, pick the {max} of highest consequence. In "secao" (section) cite file + exact heading where the answer lives; in "explicacao" (explanation), why the correct one is correct (2 sentences).

prompt.sdd.gate.answer:
Evaluate a free answer to a gate quiz question. It is only correct if it reaches the same conclusion as the correct option, for the same reason.
Question: {question}
Options: {options}
Correct: {correct}. Why: {why}
{ofUser} answer (voice transcript): «{text}»
"comentario" (comment): one sentence saying what was right or what was missing, without revealing the correct option.

prompt.sdd.gate.explain:
Assisted reading of the consolidation cycle{rulesRef}: read with {theUser} only the section where the point that slipped lives, step by step, answering whatever {he} ask. Do not present the whole artifact again.
Points that slipped: {missed}
{ofUser} question: «{question}»
"fala" (speech): up to 90 words, to be heard.
{chatRules}
{speechRules}

prompt.sdd.gate.round:
New round of the Gate {gate} quiz of {ref} on the same point that slipped, with NEW questions (not the same ones reshuffled), plus whatever is still pending.
Points: {points}
Already asked: {asked}
Re-read {artifact}: the section may have changed.
{quizRules}

prompt.sdd.qa.ask:
{ofUser} or QA's question in the hand-off of {ref} (voice transcript): «{question}»
"fala" (speech): up to 90 words.
{chatRules}
{speechRules}

prompt.sdd.retro.main:
{ofUser} weekly retro, by voice, from {from} to {to}. You lead it.
Base: the summary below ({base}). You may read specs{docsRef} to understand a point; do not invent a fact that is not in the summary or in what you read.
{focus}
"fala" (speech): an opening of up to {words} words. "numeros" (numbers): 3 to 6 counts for the week; "valor" (value) is just the number (e.g. "2", "4") and the context goes in "rotulo" (label, up to 8 words). Each item of "funcionou" (worked), "travou" (stuck) and "retrabalho" (rework) with concrete evidence (issue, date).
{improvements}
Summary of the week: {digest}
{speechRules}

prompt.sdd.retro.ask:
In the retro, {theUser} said (voice transcript): «{question}»
Answer, go deeper or propose; "fala" (speech) up to 90 words.
{chatRules}
{speechRules}

prompt.sdd.reentry.ask:
{ofUser} question in the re-entry of {ref} (voice transcript): «{question}»
"fala" (speech): up to 90 words.
{chatRules}
{speechRules}

prompt.sdd.discussion.main:
Review of MR {mr} (issue {ref}, {title}). Explain to {toUser} ONE open discussion from the reviewer and propose a draft of {his} reply. Do not publish anything.
{specLine}
Location: {where}.
Discussion {id}, oldest to newest:
{notes}
{viewHint}
"ponto" (point): what the reviewer is asking or questioning, in one sentence. "precisa_codigo" (needs code): true if meeting it requires changing the code.
"fala" (speech): up to 90 words, to be heard: the point, whether the reviewer is right from what you read and what {theUser} needs to decide.
"rascunho" (draft): {ofUser} reply to the reviewer, in English, direct and courteous, up to 80 words, in the first person. Do not claim that something was fixed, tested or committed if you did not see it; if it requires a change, write the intention ("I will adjust X"). If information is missing, leave the part in [brackets] for {he} to fill in.
"texto" (text) explains the point; the draft reply goes only in "rascunho", without repeating it in the text.
{chatRules}
{speechRules}

prompt.sdd.agents.summarize:
Summarize each project below in ONE short sentence (up to 25 words), for someone setting up development-support agents: what the project is and what context it offers the agents. Use only the data below; do not invent.
Projects: {projects}
"resumos" (summaries): one entry per project, with the "id" exactly as it is and the "resumo" (summary).
